From: Rolando Trevino <122947376+rolotrealanis98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:17:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] ui: follow the desktop's text size, with a scale setting

The engine applies GTK text-scaling-factor to text alone, which shrinks type but
not widgets, so the Omarchy text size and the app's phone-sized layout disagreed.
Scale the whole UI instead: the app is laid out at window/scale and scaled back,
and the engine's text factor is replaced by a font-size multiplier. The automatic
scale makes the body text (14 px) as large as the desktop's interface text
(12 px at Omarchy's current size), follows omarchy-display-text-size live, and
Desktop Settings gets Match Desktop Text Size, Interface Scale and Font Size.
BB_UI_SCALE and BB_FONT_SCALE override both for measuring.
